Kani mutant m1: index_2d_runtime flattens row * width + col into the witness at mint time
(the historical bug), so a witness minted from one slice's grid aliases
another thread's cell when resolved through a slice of a different width.

Must be killed by: kani_proofs::p3_cross_slice_no_alias_b1x1, kani_proofs::p3_cross_slice_no_alias_b32x8

diff --git a/cuda-oxide/crates/cuda-device/src/thread.rs b/cuda-oxide/crates/cuda-device/src/thread.rs
--- a/cuda-oxide/crates/cuda-device/src/thread.rs
+++ b/cuda-oxide/crates/cuda-device/src/thread.rs
@@ -764,7 +764,7 @@
         if row > u32::MAX as usize {
             return None;
         }
-        let raw = super::pack_runtime_2d_coords(row, col);
+        let raw = row * row_stride + col;
         Some(unsafe { ThreadIndex::new(raw, true, scope) })
     }
 
